# Homebrew
Brewfile.lock.json

# Backup files
*.backup
*.bak

# Python
__pycache__/

# uv debris. This repo is not a uv project — pyproject.toml carries only
# [tool.pytest.ini_options] and no [project] table — but uv cannot tell, so any
# bare `uv run` with the repo as its CWD writes both of these. `uv.lock` pins
# nothing (three lines, no packages) and was deleted deliberately in #793,
# because a lockfile present is what advertises a uv project and sends the next
# reader to `uv run pytest` instead of the bare command everything here uses.
# It came back through a blanket `git add -A` that swept it into an unrelated
# commit, which is the accident these two lines close.
#
# .venv/ is listed for completeness rather than need: uv writes `.venv/.gitignore`
# holding `*`, so the directory hides itself and never reaches `git status`.
# That self-concealment is exactly why it is worth naming here — it is the half
# of the debris nobody notices, and a reader who deletes one should know about
# the other.
uv.lock
.venv/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Claude Code — .claude/ is tracked, the same way `otto-workbench ai init`
# scaffolds it into every other repo. Its machine-local files are listed in
# .claude/.gitignore.

ai/memory/

# Editor files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Generated AI context (regenerated by setup and hooks)
ai/guidelines/rules/tools.generated*.md
ai/guidelines/rules/git.generated.md

# Worktree-local state directories
ignore/
.workbench/

# Archives — build artifacts (e.g. build-otto-ai-tools-tarball writes to the CWD)
*.tar.gz
*.zip

# Superpowers plugin artifacts
.superpowers/
docs/superpowers/
